  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify a dependency-pinned Statistics NuGet candidate from eight original sources and a published exact Quantities package, using eighteen independent numerical/refusal binary checks without publishing.",
    "value": "Build an immutable candidate using a temporary source-linked project with one exact dw.quantities PackageReference; verify physical dependency hashes, source lockfile, package manifest and isolated consumer with unchanged source bytes.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "The original Statistics project retains its historical dw.quantities ProjectReference and 0.4.0-preview.6 version; only the temporary pack projection may use the exact published Quantities package.",
      "Statistics becomes a candidate only, with an execution-time calendar version and original archive/DLL hashes recorded in F24; no publication or reservation is authorized.",
      "Existing seven independently published Math packages, source/lockfile SHA-256, 541 completed native nodes and F1-F23 evidence are preserved; public/rollback/cross-repo claims remain excluded.",
      "RS157 preselection invocation run-next-20261106T101031Z-c4980352814d6788 was refused before allocation: staged StatisticsBinaryConsumer.cs was required before installation. The exact file-existence guard now runs after staging; no attempt or product mutation occurred.",
      "RS157 preselection run-next-20261106T113150Z-1f64471f7e8884e0 failed before allocation: F1 inventory used --no-build with no executable in disposable checkout. The candidate now restores/builds pinned F1 from NUGET_LOCAL before two observations; eleven inner receipts, no source/feed mutation.",
      "RS157 preselection run-next-20261106T130251Z-9b983d561929ebf6 failed before allocation: consumer-build CS8629 at nullable SampleVariance.Value. Same 18-oracle fixture now uses SampleVariance ?? throw for compiler-proven nonnull value; no source/feed mutation."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After successful RS157 candidate qualification, rehearse its immutable publisher in a disposable feed; an explicit owner release and subsequent physical readback remain separate gates.",
